CM_ BO_ 2286157824 "Miss this for 1 s and the BMU drops HV";
CM_ SG_ 2286157824 ECU_F_PrechargeReq "The comp25 BMU doesn't look at this, it only reads 0x1080C001";
CM_ SG_ 2286157824 ECU_F_HvOffReq "Spare, always 0 till the rules side is sorted";
CM_ SG_ 2286157824 ECU_Uptime "Goes back to 0 on a reset so you can spot it in the log";
CM_ SG_ 2424356865 ECU_C25_State "40 is what makes the comp25 BMU precharge";
CM_ SG_ 2281963520 BMU_F_HbEcu "BMU can't hear our heartbeat";
CM_ SG_ 2281963520 BMU_F_PrechargeTimeout "comp25 sets this on any trip with the contactors shut, not just a slow precharge";
CM_ SG_ 2281963520 BMU_PackState "comp25 never fills this";
CM_ SG_ 2281963520 BMU_SOC "comp25 never fills this";
CM_ SG_ 2418327552 BMU_F_HbEcu "BMU can't hear our heartbeat";
CM_ SG_ 2418327552 BMU_F_PrechargeTimeout "comp25 sets this on any trip with the contactors shut, not just a slow precharge";
CM_ SG_ 2418327552 BMU_PackState "comp25 never fills this";
CM_ SG_ 2418327552 BMU_SOC "comp25 never fills this";
CM_ BO_ 2298740736 "Only LoopClosed decides anything, the segment bits are for humans";
CM_ BO_ 2164260864 "Error priority so it beats everything else onto the bus";
CM_ SG_ 2290122752 SHDN_OldLines "Always 0, the old firmware's union is really a struct";
CM_ BO_ 2307129344 "Only on the bus when charging";
CM_ BO_ 2555117568 "Anything that touches outputs, cal or params is refused while DRIVING. Reply goes back on whichever bus asked";
CM_ SG_ 2555117568 DBG_ReqArg "Float bits for PARAM_SET, OUTPUT_DUTY and the CAL_ ones";
